=== foundation rules ===

## Foundational Context

This application is a Laravel Backend and Next.js frontend application. Package versions are auto-generated from composer.lock and pnpm-lock.yaml. Respect these versions when consulting docs or suggesting code.

@.cursor/deps-versions.md
@.devin/deps-versions.md

- node - 20.x (recommended; not pinned in project)
- pnpm - v9

## Information Gathering (≥90% Rule)

- Before starting implementation, assess whether you have at least 90% of the information needed to fulfil the request (scope, constraints, edge cases, existing patterns).
- If you lack critical details (e.g. which file/API, environment, auth rules, acceptance criteria), ask the user concise, targeted questions until you reach that threshold. Do not guess or assume.
- Once you have enough information, perform a **confirmation step**: in 2–4 short sentences, state exactly what you understood (goal, scope, constraints) and ask the user to confirm before proceeding (e.g. "Confermi che proceda così?" / "Confirm before I continue?").

## Solution Quality & Sources

- Base all solutions on verified practices: official docs (Laravel, Next.js, React, PHP, Node), security advisories (OWASP, CVE), and established patterns already used in this codebase.
- Prioritise in this order: **security** (no injection, proper auth/sanctum, validation, escaping), **performance** (queries, caching, bundle size, N+1), **code cleanliness** (DRY, naming, structure). When in doubt, prefer the safer or more maintainable option.

## Comments Language

- Write **all** code comments in **English only**, regardless of the language of the user's prompt or the surrounding UI/copy. This applies to inline comments, block comments, docblocks, and TODO/FIXME notes.

